title: 'feat: VersionedCall primitive + version-checking for stored calls (#1138)'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/1138

    Introduces the `VersionedCall<Call>` primitive in `sp-runtime` (an opaque `Call` plus the
    `transaction_version` it was created at, with `validate_version`/`into_inner` helpers and a
    `VersionMismatchError`) and integrates version-checking into the pallets that store calls for
    later execution, so that a runtime upgrade changing call encoding/semantics cannot silently
    change the effect of an already-stored call.

    pallet-scheduler:
    - Tasks created through the user-facing extrinsics record the runtime's `transaction_version`.
      At dispatch, a version mismatch drops the task with a `CallVersionMismatch` event instead of
      executing it. This is opt-in per task (stored as `Scheduled::maybe_transaction_version`):
      tasks scheduled via the internal `schedule::v2`/`v3` traits record no version and are
      unaffected, preserving existing behaviour for pallet bookkeeping (e.g. referenda alarms).
    - Migration `migration::v5::MigrateV4ToV5` upgrades existing agendas (existing tasks unchecked).

    frame-support: adds a non-breaking `schedule_named_versioned` method to the `schedule::v3::Named`
    trait (default implementation delegates to `schedule_named`), so callers can opt a deferred call
    into version-checking. The scheduler overrides it to record the current `transaction_version`.

    pallet-collective: `ProposalOf` now stores the proposal wrapped in a `VersionedCall` (keyed by
    the hash of the bare proposal, so identity/voting are unchanged). On approval, a version mismatch
    drops the proposal with a `ProposalVersionMismatch` event instead of executing it. Migration
    `migrations::v5::MigrateToV5` wraps existing proposals.

    pallet-democracy / pallet-referenda: route referendum enactment through
    `schedule_named_versioned`, so an enactment whose `transaction_version` changed before it runs is
    dropped by the scheduler. No storage change or migration is needed in these pallets (the version
    lives on the scheduler task); internal referenda alarms remain unversioned.

    The in-repo runtimes using pallet-scheduler / pallet-collective are wired with the respective
    `MigrateV4ToV5` / `MigrateToV5` migration in their `Migrations` tuple.

    Multisig and lottery are intentionally not covered: they do not persist a full call across blocks
    (multisig stores only a call hash, lottery only call indices), so `VersionedCall` does not apply.
crates:
- name: sp-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: frame-support
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-scheduler
  bump: major
- name: pallet-collective
  bump: major
- name: pallet-democracy
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-referenda
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-alliance
  bump: none
- name: kitchensink-runtime
  bump: major
- name: collectives-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: major
